# Every course in Numa's public curriculum catalog (https://numaschool.com/curriculum),
# fetched verbatim from its public GET /api/curriculum/catalog endpoint (629 courses,
# paginated via limit/offset) so title/provider/subject/grade/credit data matches the
# live site exactly. `category` is derived deterministically from Numa's `subject.name`,
# `difficulty` from its `level` (elementary/middle/high -> BEGINNER/INTERMEDIATE/ADVANCED),
# and `tags` / the description's trailing line carry the provider, credit hours, and grade
# range since the Course model has no dedicated fields for them. `subject` and
# `grade_label` are kept as their own keys (not just parsed back out of `tags`) because
# `_create_course_content` uses them as ground truth for the quiz questions it generates.
# The per-course platform content itself (module/lesson/assignment/quiz counts, amount,
# and the quiz's distractor choices) is randomly but deterministically generated by
# `_create_course_content` — Numa's catalog doesn't expose that content, only metadata.
